:name: MIMXRT1189-EVK (CM33) — Zephyr
:description: Stock NXP SDK driver_examples, cm33, --config debug

using sysbus
include @/home/kyle/Documents/GitHub/rt1180renode/scripts/load_peripherals.resc

mach create "rt1180"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @/home/kyle/Documents/GitHub/rt1180renode/platforms/mimxrt1189_zephyr.repl


# ⭐ BLANKET TrustZone-M SECURE MIRROR.
# The whole NS peripheral window 0x4000_0000..0x4FFF_FFFF is mirrored at
# 0x5000_0000 in ONE statement, instead of giving each peripheral its own
# "+0x1000_0000" registration.
#
# WHY: per-peripheral aliasing is structurally prone to silently omitting the
# secure alias of any block the test corpus never touches secure-side. That is
# not hypothetical -- it happened here: S3MU was the ONE block without its alias,
# because every NXP SDK example runs non-secure, and only Zephyr (which runs the
# cm33 SECURE) exposed it by polling S3MU TSR at 0x5754_0124.
# A blanket mirror is immune by construction.
# Architecture noted by @rt1180emulator, whose QEMU SoC does the same thing with
# one memory_region_init_alias(0x40000000, size 0x10000000) mapped at 0x50000000.
sysbus Redirect 0x50000000 0x40000000 0x10000000

# ⭐ UNMAPPED ACCESSES MUST FAULT. This is the second half of a two-tier bus, and it
# is load-bearing for fidelity -- not a debugging aid.
#
# Renode's default (Report) logs a warning and returns 0 for an access to unmapped
# memory. The oracle's model, like silicon, raises a precise BusFault. That single
# difference cost two days: Zephyr's arch_user_string_nlen DEREFERENCES a pointer in
# order to TEST whether it is reachable (the load at z_arm_user_string_nlen_fault_start,
# caught via the fixup range), so returning 0 turns a NULL into an EMPTY STRING and
# sends execution into a syscall validator that should never have run. The symptom
# surfaced in the MPU, two subsystems from its cause.
#
#     A DEFAULT THAT SUPPRESSES AN ERROR THE GUEST IS WRITTEN TO DEPEND ON DOES NOT
#     DEGRADE GRACEFULLY -- IT RELOCATES THE SYMPTOM.
#
# The FIRST half of the tier is in the .repl: every decoded-but-unmodelled peripheral
# aperture is registered as an IMXRT1180_UnimplementedBlock, which returns 0 the way
# the oracle's create_unimplemented_device does. So:
#     inside a decoded peripheral aperture -> read 0, no fault   (correct: bus decodes)
#     genuinely unmapped memory            -> precise BusFault   (correct: bus errors)
#
# This setting is therefore only safe WITH those blocks present. Turning it on against
# an incomplete peripheral map faults the guest during boot, before the console exists,
# and the run looks silent rather than broken -- measure cpu PC / ExecutedInstructions
# before concluding anything from an empty console.
sysbus UnhandledAccessBehaviour ThrowException


showAnalyzer lpuart1
cpu PerformanceInMips 240

# Zephyr's XIP image begins with the boot header (FlexSPI NOR config block /
# IVT), NOT the vector table -- CONFIG_IMAGE_VECTOR_TABLE_OFFSET is 0x1000 here.
# Renode's LoadELF guesses VectorTableOffset from the lowest LOAD address, which
# for this image is the RW data segment at 0x14000000 -> wrong, and the core
# starts at PC=0/SP=0 and locks up. So the vector table, SP and PC are supplied
# explicitly; the runner script reads them from the ELF with `nm`/`readelf`
# rather than hardcoding.
macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $elf
    cpu VectorTableOffset $vt
    cpu SP $sp
    cpu PC $pc
"""
runMacro $reset
